    "# AI & Machine Learning: Code, Train & Deploy\n",
    "## Week 14 — Advanced Music Intelligence: Time Series, NLP, and Exploration\n",
    "\n",
    "**Syllabus focus:** time series analysis; natural language processing; reinforcement learning; ethical AI and bias.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business context:** Listener behavior changes over time, and a recommendation system must decide when to exploit known preferences and when to explore promising but uncertain music.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Capstone deliverable:** A recommendation strategy that balances engagement with exploration of underexposed artists.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Learning objectives\n",
    "- understand time-based listening patterns\n",
    "- reason about exploration vs exploitation\n",
    "- connect recommendation logic to decision theory\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import random\n",
    "\n",
    "actions = ['mainstream hit', 'niche artist', 'new release']\n",
    "rewards = {'mainstream hit': 0.80, 'niche artist': 0.63, 'new release': 0.58}\n",
    "\n",
    "selected = random.choice(actions)\n",
    "print('Selected action:', selected)\n",
    "print('Expected reward:', rewards[selected])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Exploration-exploitation framing\n",
    "\n",
    "The platform has to decide whether to keep recommending music that already works (exploit) or to try lesser-known artists with untapped potential (explore). The best recommendation strategies often combine both.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Practice task\n",
    "Write a short strategy memo explaining when a platform should prefer a familiar artist and when it should take a risk on a niche artist.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
